    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The original is simple but can be made more understandable by: removing unused imports, naming the expected value, and adding assertion messages that explain the Soundex breakdown and why each form produces the same result.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes unused imports, introduces a named constant `expectedSoundexCode` to avoid repeating the magic string `\"B312\"`, and adds a detailed Javadoc comment explaining the H/W rule and full encoding breakdown, plus per-assertion messages that clarify what each case is verifying."
